{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1143454-perfected-lithium","id":1143454,"title":"Perfected Lithium?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-24T07:50:53-07:00","id":1143454,"title":"Perfected Lithium?","content":"So my players have discovered perfected Metals... they've done mysteries on perfected versions of iron, silver and copper. Now they're getting creative. One of them is currently purifying the Lithium from a car battery so that they can perfect it. Any ideas for what the perfected version on Lithium should be like? As an alkali metal i'm probably gonna go for explosive/extremely reactive but how about supernal semiotics and associations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T08:04:49-07:00","id":1143459,"title":"","content":"It might not do anything, apparently the attempts to perfect other materials has met with limited results according to the preview. Lithium by itself doesn't seem to be all that remarkable, it seems most applications of it are used as part of an alloy, compound, or as a catalyst. It might form a different kind of amagalm than Hermium, maybe one that's reactive with non-Perfected materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T08:24:06-07:00","id":1143463,"title":"","content":"It would go boom. I mean, a big boom. Lithium is very reactive as is- so a perfected version of it would explode that unless the mage is question was careful enough to contain it properly and put their shields up, they are burned meat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T11:00:30-07:00","id":1143512,"title":"","content":"As a chemistry student I disagree with the big boom. Lithium is very reactive, but it doesn't just go boom. Of the alkalimetals it reacts the slowest. If your players were going for Rubidium or Caesium, then an immediate boom on contact with air would be very appropriate.<br /> <br /> BUT you also need to consider that, given what we've seen in the preview, perfected materials seem to be relativly inert. Both mercury and lead, which tend to be quite reactive, are alot less so in their perfected forms.<br /> <br /> Given all these things I would personally say that perfected Lithium, unlike normal Lithium, does NOT react with air. However when specifically reacted with another substance it is an absolute beast of an reductive agent, posessing a highly negative normal potential. Which incidentially would allow one to produce very powerful batteries of it (especially when paired with perfected fluorine. I hope you have a very very high potency version of Alchemists Touch on when handling perfected Fluorine however <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T11:18:33-07:00","id":1143516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1143454-perfected-lithium?p=1143512#post1143512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a chemistry student I disagree with the big boom. Lithium is very reactive, but it doesn't just go boom. Of the alkalimetals it reacts the slowest. If your players were going for Rubidium or Caesium, then an immediate boom on contact with air would be very appropriate.<br /> <br /> BUT you also need to consider that, given what we've seen in the preview, perfected materials seem to be relativly inert. Both mercury and lead, which tend to be quite reactive, are alot less so in their perfected forms.<br /> <br /> Given all these things I would personally say that perfected Lithium, unlike normal Lithium, does NOT react with air. However when specifically reacted with another substance it is an absolute beast of an reductive agent, posessing a highly negative normal potential. Which incidentially would allow one to produce very powerful batteries of it (especially when paired with perfected fluorine. I hope you have a very very high potency version of Alchemists Touch on when handling perfected Fluorine however <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, it is the least reactive one- but this is Mage, and we are talking about symbolism in here. Lithium, in many ways, symbolise the Alkali metals, and the process which perfects metals enhance those symbols, so as the alkalies are defined through their enhanced reactivity (unlike lead or mercury, which may be reactive but they don't represent those symbols), the Lithium, the &quot;symbol&quot; of the alkalies, would become much more reactive than the usual. Caesium and Rubidium, while much more reactive in real life, would be much harder to be perfected as, through the eyes of a Mage's cosmology, may not be able to be perfected at all, as the symbols which define them may see them as nothing more than a &quot;much more reactive Lithium&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, while science has its place in the process of metal perfection, this is magic- and we should also consider the way magic work in the setting in order to decide the outcome pf the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T11:37:28-07:00","id":1143519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1143454-perfected-lithium?p=1143516#post1143516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, it is the least reactive one- but this is Mage, and we are talking about symbolism in here. Lithium, in many ways, symbolise the Alkali metals, and the process which perfects metals enhance those symbols, so as the alkalies are defined through their enhanced reactivity (unlike lead or mercury, which may be reactive but they don't represent those symbols), the Lithium, the &quot;symbol&quot; of the alkalies, would become much more reactive than the usual. Caesium and Rubidium, while much more reactive in real life, would be much harder to be perfected as, through the eyes of a Mage's cosmology, may not be able to be perfected at all, as the symbols which define them may see them as nothing more than a &quot;much more reactive Lithium&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, while science has its place in the process of metal perfection, this is magic- and we should also consider the way magic work in the setting in order to decide the outcome pf the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does Lithium as the least reactive of the alkali metals symbolize the reactivity of the alkalimetals in general? Sorry but that doesn't make any sense. In general I don't think Lithium is the symbol of the alkalimetals at all, people are way more familiar with Sodium and Potassium on average. And in general what people are familar with doesn't matter in Awakening. I see no reason why the supernal groups these Elements together as alakali metals to begin with, they're probably their own distinct symbols. You could now argue that natural abundance might play a role, but the high supernal importance of lead flies directly in the face of that.<br /> <br /> In short: Neither Lithium nor Caesium are dependant on a supernal version of alkaline metals. They are derived from symbolism of their own independently. That humans group them together as alkaline elements and tend to think of that group rather than the independent elements sounds to me more like an element of the lie muddying supernal truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T12:13:32-07:00","id":1143533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1143454-perfected-lithium?p=1143519#post1143519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why does Lithium as the least reactive of the alkali metals symbolize the reactivity of the alkalimetals in general? Sorry but that doesn't make any sense. In general I don't think Lithium is the symbol of the alkalimetals at all, people are way more familiar with Sodium and Potassium on average. And in general what people are familar with doesn't matter in Awakening. I see no reason why the supernal groups these Elements together as alakali metals to begin with, they're probably their own distinct symbols. You could now argue that natural abundance might play a role, but the high supernal importance of lead flies directly in the face of that.<br /> <br /> In short: Neither Lithium nor Caesium are dependant on a supernal version of alkaline metals. They are derived from symbolism of their own independently. That humans group them together as alkaline elements and tend to think of that group rather than the independent elements sounds to me more like an element of the lie muddying supernal truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason I called Lithium as the &quot;representative&quot; of the Alkalies is because it is a part of what is sometimes called the &quot;representative elements&quot;- you know, the first and second rows of the table. While because of their atomic properties they are quit different from the rest of the table, they are considered as &quot;laying the ground&quot; for the next elements in their column. Hence the concept of Lithium as the &quot;symbol of the alkalies&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the fact that in Awakening there is not &quot;mind shapes reality&quot;- again, I know that. However, Awakening's cosmology is Platonic, and as such reality is only the shadows cast by the Supernal symbols. The way I interpreted that cosmology is that just as there symbols for each of the alkalies, those symbols are, by themselves, incarnations of much deeper symbols, such the the symbol of the alkali metals. And Lithium, as the &quot;representative element&quot; of the alkali metals, is much closer to the symbol of the alkalies in general. Hence the concept of perfected Lithium becoming the &quot;symbol of alkalies&quot;, and the rest of the alkalies being defined through the symbol of Lithium.<br /> <br /> In sort, the way I see it, the symbol of Lithium is much closer to the symbol of the alkalies than any other alkali metals, and as the properties it express in the fallen map themselves in a way that humanity would place it in the top of the alkali metals, and as such make it the representative of the alkali metals. It is not human awareness which decides the importance of the symbols- but it is the human mind which collect those symbols and put them in such a way that it recognize the patterns in the fallen universe, and tries to adapt those symbols into a way which is the closest to the Supernal- even while it is unaware of its actions. The periodic table, which is actually a collection of symbols used in order to name every material on the face of earth, is such an example of humanity unknowingly recognizing the way the Supernal symbols express themselves in the Fallen patterns.<br /> <br /> In sort, as it much more of the philosophical debate about the meaning of the Supernal symbols in Mage than about the actual properties of the element, I'm not going into delving for into that argument- I have just wished to present my opinion on the subject, and as your interpretation pf Mage's cosmology decides how perfected Lithium would be presented in the setting, unless some canon rules would be provided for such case I don't see a way we could agree about the subject :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T12:41:01-07:00","id":1143548,"title":"","content":"It would <i>obviously</i> intensify Life and Mind magic dealing with calm and emotions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithium_(medication)\" target=\"_blank\">I mean, obviously.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:01:11-07:00","id":1143553,"title":"","content":"Perfect lithium goes boom. Perfect Caesium goes boom <i>even faster</i>, but it's very hard to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:23:18-07:00","id":1143562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1143454-perfected-lithium?p=1143533#post1143533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In sort, as it much more of the philosophical debate about the meaning of the Supernal symbols in Mage than about the actual properties of the element, I'm not going into delving for into that argument- I have just wished to present my opinion on the subject, and as your interpretation pf Mage's cosmology decides how perfected Lithium would be presented in the setting, unless some canon rules would be provided for such case I don't see a way we could agree about the subject :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see where you're coming from and it's certainly one valid approach to the issue. The one thing that kind of contradicts it in my mind is the presence of the canonical perfected metals. Lead is not at the top of the periodic table at all, but has intense magical symbolism due to its connection to Stygia, leading me to believe that the placement on the periodic table is not a safe indicator of the weight of supernal symbolism an element carries at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:34:16-07:00","id":1143567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1143454-perfected-lithium?p=1143548#post1143548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would <i>obviously</i> intensify Life and Mind magic dealing with calm and emotions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lithium_(medication)&amp;quot;]I</a> mean, obviously.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it would make someone super mellow, possibly while also setting them on fire?<br /> <br /> Considering the above, I could see burning Perfect Lithium as a powerful meditative tool/Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-24-2017, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}